Let \operatorname{H}_{n}(\subset \operatorname{M}_{n}( denote the \mathbb {R}-subspace of hermitian matrices. For X\in \operatorname{M}_{n}( let\operatorname{Re}X=\frac{1}{2} (X+X^*),\qquad \operatorname{Im}X=\frac{1}{2i}(X-X^*).Then \operatorname{Re}X,\operatorname{Im}X\in \operatorname{H}_{n}( and X=\operatorname{Re}X+i\operatorname{Im}X.Lemma 2.1 
