Propagation-based X-ray phase contrast tomography: Newton-Kaczmarz iterations for this problem with L^2-data-fidelity and Sobolev-W^{1,2}-penalty, as first proposed in \cite {MaretzkeEtAl2016OptExpr}, are of the form \begin{align}
f_{k+1} = \operatornamewithlimits{argmin}_{f \in L^2(\Omega ) } \big \Vert F \left( {P}_{j_k} (f_k) \right) + F^{\prime }[{P}_{j_k} (f_k) ] \left( {P}_{j_k}(f-f_k) \right) - g_{j_k}^{\textup {obs}} \big \Vert _{L^2}^2 \\+ \alpha \left( (1-\gamma ) \Vert f-f_k \Vert _{L^2}^2 + \gamma \Vert \nabla ( f-f_k ) \Vert _{L^2}^2\right). 
\end{align}
If we take \mathcal {S}(p):= \Vert F \left( {P}_{j_k} (f_k) \right) + F^{\prime }[{P}_{j_k} (f_k) ] \left( p - {P}_{j_k} (f_k) \right) - g_{j_k}^{\textup {obs}} \Vert _{L^2}^2,
(\ref {eq:NewtonKaczmarzPCT}) matches the setting of {thm:W12SART}. Hence, within the minor approximation discussed in the end of §\ref {SS:GradPenalties}, the minimizer may be computed via the GenSART-scheme
\begin{align}
f_{k+1} \approx f_k + {P}_{j_k}^\ast \bigg ( u_{j_k}^{-1/2} \cdot \operatornamewithlimits{argmin}_{p \in {L^2({\mathbb {D}\!_{{j_k}}})}} \big \Vert F^{\prime }[{P}_{j_k} (f_k) ]\big ( u_{j_k}^{1/2} \cdot p \big ) - r_{j_k} \big \Vert _{L^2}^2 \\+ \alpha _k (1-\gamma ) \Vert p \Vert _{L^2}^2 + \alpha _k \gamma \big \Vert u_{j_k}^{1/2} \cdot \nabla _{\mathbb {D}} \big ( u_{j_k}^{-1/2 } \cdot p \big ) \big \Vert _{L^2}^2 \bigg ) \end{align}
with residual r_{j_k} := g_{j_k}^{\textup {obs}} - F \left( {P}_{j_k} (f_k) \right).
The quadratic optimization problem in (\ref {eq:PCTSART}) can be solved for example by a conjugate-gradient method applied to the normal equation.
}

