}We may now apply {thm:apriori} along with standard Bramble-Hilbert arguments (see~\cite [Corollary~3.6]{gopalakrishnan2014analysis} for details) to obtain convergence rates dictated by the following corollary to {thm:apriori}.
}\begin{}

Let h= \operatornamewithlimits{\vphantom{p}max}_{K\in _h} \mathrm {diam}(K), d=2,3, and let the assumptions of {thm:apriori,prop:LM} hold.
Let \vec{v}_h = (\vec{p}_h, v_h) \in {V}_h and \vec{\lambda }_h = (\vec{\zeta }_h, \lambda _h, \widehat{\zeta }_{n,h}, \widehat{\lambda }_h) \in {U}_h be the DPG* solutions to {eq:DPGstarApprox}, with G(\vec{\mu }) = (f,\mu ).
Let e\in H_0^1() satisfy -\Delta e = v+2f.
Then
\begin{align}
\Vert \vec{v}- \vec{v}_h \Vert _{V}+ \Vert \vec{\lambda }- \vec{\lambda }_h \Vert _{U}&\le C h^s
\big (\Vert v\Vert _{H^{s+2}()} + \Vert e\Vert _{H^{s+2}()}\big )
\,,

\end{align}
for all 1/2 < s < p+1.
\end{}Note that the left-hand side of the inequalities in thm:apriori,cor:DPG*PoissonConvergenceRates coincide.
Therefore, our proof proceeds by showing that \operatornamewithlimits{\vphantom{p}inf}_{\vec{\nu } \in {V}_h}\Vert \vec{v} - \vec{\nu } \Vert _{V}^2 + \operatornamewithlimits{\vphantom{p}inf}_{\vec{\mu } \in {U}_h} \Vert \vec{\lambda } - \vec{\mu } \Vert _{U} is bounded from above by the right-hand side of eq:DPG*PoissonConvergenceRatesIneq.First notice that \Vert \vec{v} - \vec{\nu } \Vert _{V}^2 = \Vert \vec{p}-\vec{\tau }\Vert _{H(\operatorname{div},_h)}^2 + \Vert v-\nu \Vert _{H^1(_h)}^2.
Therefore, the following inequality, \operatornamewithlimits{\vphantom{p}inf}_{\vec{\nu }\in {V}_h}\Vert \vec{v}- \vec{\nu }\Vert _{V}^2 \le C h^{s} (\Vert \vec{p}\Vert _{H^{s+1}()} + \Vert v\Vert _{H^{s+1}()}), is immediate upon substituting {\vec{\nu }= \prod _{K\in _h}(_{\operatorname{div}}^K\vec{p},_{\operatorname{grad}}^K v)}, where _{\operatorname{div}}^K: H(\operatorname{div},K) \rightarrow \vec{x}P_{p}(K) + P_{p}(K)^d and _{\operatorname{grad}}^K:H^1(K)\rightarrow P_{p+1}(K) are the local Raviart–Thomas and nodal interpolation operators, for each element K\in _h.

